\begin_layout Section
How to run the experiments
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The steps below summarize how to repeat the experiments.
 The detailed instructions for Linux are in the file 
\family typewriter
txt/How-To-Deploy-Schrodinger-Memory.txt
\family default
 of the repository.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Clone the repository from the link in Table A.1.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Run the script 
\family typewriter
init.sh
\family default
,
 which creates a virtual environment with Python 3.9 and installs the required packages (
\family typewriter
PyQt6
\family default
,
 
\family typewriter
Qiskit
\family default
,
 
\family typewriter
Qiskit Aer
\family default
,
 
\family typewriter
Matplotlib
\family default
 and the module 
\family typewriter
qiskit-ibm-runtime
\family default
).
 Then activate the environment with the command 
\family typewriter
source .venv/bin/activate
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Open the file 
\family typewriter
src/config.py
\family default
 and set the value of 
\family typewriter
BACKEND_MODE
\family default
.
 The value 
\family typewriter
"simulator"
\family default
 runs the game locally and needs no account.
 The value 
\family typewriter
"ibm"
\family default
 runs it on a real IBM processor,
 and it is the value used in the tagged release.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
For the real processor,
 create an account on the IBM Quantum Platform and save the credentials once on your computer,
 with the channel set to 
\family typewriter
ibm_quantum_platform
\family default
.
 The access token is never stored in the repository.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Run one of the five experiment files according with the correct file name,
 for example 
\family typewriter
python src/exp1_no_entanglement_random_qubits.py
\family default
.
\end_layout

